<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">University of San Francisco Xavier</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as University of Saint Francis Xavier</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-francisco">San Francisco</a> Xavier in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sucre">Sucre</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a>, was founded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a> in 1624 and is one of the oldest universities in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>. In the late colonial period its law faculty and academy educated many leaders of the independence movements of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-peru">Upper Peru</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">Río de la Plata</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/university-of-san-francisco-xavier.jpg" alt="University of San Francisco Xavier" width="320" height="367" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Universidad de Chuquisaca · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chuquisacantiguo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
